            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A dome swamp is a swamp which occurs in a depression where deeper waters at the centre of the swamp allow  trees to grow taller relative to those in shallower regions of the depression. This creates a dome-like shape.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>The logical def should be improved with the idea of a vegetation unit growing in a depression expressed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>dome swamp</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


